; Test 09: options.  blitz2 without a file, DEFAULTS (menu 0 3; TED closes
; and reopens its screen), tab stop gadget 6 = 8 + GADGETUP on it (TED
; applies the numbers only on the string gadget's GADGETUP, like Return -
; OK alone keeps them: stage 1 saved tabstop 2), OK (gadget 26), QUIT
; (savedefs -> L:blitzeditor.opts = TEDRUN:L).  Compared: option file
; A<->B, dump.
; @source none
; @est 5
; @expect opts blitzeditor.opts tabstop=8
timeout 10
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
menu 0 3
wait req "OK" "CANCEL"
str 6 "8"
gad 6
dump defaults
gad 26
wait screen
dump after
menu 0 9
wait exit
